-- title:
--   Places of a constant-field extension are determined by their centre
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $K$ algebraically closed of characteristic $0$, and assume `IsCurveOver K F`: every nonzero $f \in F$ has a principal divisor, i.e. a degree-zero divisor whose value at each place is $\operatorname{ord}_v f$, each place of $F/K$ has residue field finite over $K$, and $\Omega[F/K]$ is free of rank $1$ over $F$. Assume also that some $x \in F$ is transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite-dimensional over $K(x)$. Let $E$ be an algebraically closed field extending $K$ and $FE$ a field equipped with compatible algebra structures over $K$, $E$ and $F$ (scalar towers $K \subseteq E \subseteq FE$ and $K \subseteq F \subseteq FE$), with `IsCurveOver E FE`, again finitely generated in the same sense over $E$, and such that the $E$-subfield of $FE$ generated by the image of $F$ is all of $FE$. Let $e \colon F \to E$ be a $K$-algebra homomorphism, and let $P$, $Q$ be places of $FE/E$, i.e. valuation subrings of $FE$ containing the image of $E$, distinct from $FE$, and principal ideal rings. If for every $f \in F$ the valuation of $f - e(f)$ in $FE$ is $< 1$ at $P$ and also at $Q$, then $P = Q$.
--
--   Classically this is the uniqueness statement in the dictionary between $E$-points of the base-changed curve $C_E = C \times_K E$ and places of the constant-field extension $FE/E$ centred at them: a place at which every element of $F$ is integral with residue prescribed by $e$ is unique, reflecting that $C_E$ is a smooth curve and hence has exactly one local ring dominating the point $e$. It supplies the uniqueness half of [`AlgebraicCurve.Place.existsUnique_valuation_sub_lt_one_of_constantFieldExtension`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Place.existsUnique_valuation_sub_lt_one_of_constantFieldExtension).
-- source:
